WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.160
When the lights went up in theaters showing
"The Batman," there was still one more riddle

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.480
left for moviegoers to solve — just what
exactly happens if you go to the website the

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.750
Riddler uses in the film?

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.940
Watch to the end of the video to find out.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.090
Oh, and it should go without saying, but major
spoilers ahead.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.369
Now, if you've already seen "The Batman,"
directed by Matt Reeves, then you know that

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:24.269
there's a lot to unpack.

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:29.259
Following Robert Pattinson as the Caped Crusader,
the movie is set in a dark Gotham brought

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:33.140
into chaos by a killer called the Riddler,
played by Paul Dano.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.290
Thanks to the heroic efforts of Batman, Catwoman,
and Lieutenant Jim Gordon, the Riddler's plan

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.460
is stopped before he can completely destroy
the city and its citizens.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:47.120
But even though the good guys win in the end,
"The Batman" still hints at there possibly

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.010
being more to come with Riddler in the future.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:53.850
Throughout the film, as our heroes attempt
to track down the Riddler, the villain leaves

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.140
puzzles for Batman to solve.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:01.820
One riddle in particular leads him to a website
with the URL of rataalada.com.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:06.640
This connects him with the Riddler live through
a simple, coded chat, through which Bruce

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.820
digs for any answers he can get out of the
criminal.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.500
While the website is a secret tool for Riddler
in "The Batman," Warner Bros. decided to actually

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.810
create the website in real life.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.909
So what happens when you head there?

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:22.630
"What the hell are you supposed to be?"

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.149
Keeping in line with the website's function
in "The Batman," rataalada.com brings you

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:31.549
into a conversation with a chatbot made to
mimic the Riddler character from the movie.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:36.759
He offers you the chance to play a game and
solve three riddles, and if you get them all

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:39.310
correct, you will unlock "the truth."

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:43.890
Fair warning though: the solutions to these
riddles aren't easy, and we aren't all experts

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.130
at riddles like Batman appears to be.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.609
Even so, in "The Batman," Bruce has some help
from Oswald Cobblepot a.k.a.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:54.369
the Penguin and Lieutenant Gordon, but in
this case, you're on your own.

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:58.380
Adding to the feeling that you're talking
to the real Riddler, a man who's an expert

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.789
at codes and technology, the website is well
aware of how much time you take between guesses,

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:08.100
whether or not you go to another tab or window
to try and look up the answers, or even if

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.980
you close the window entirely and return later
to try again.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.320
If you think you're smart enough to conquer
these three riddles and claim the prize, you

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.490
can head to the website and see what you unlock.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.520
"Who are you, under there?"

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.940
Before the movie's release, the site featured
riddles that would unlock promotional material,

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.680
like police sketches of Batman from the Gotham
City Police Department.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:33.400
But now that the movie has debuted, the reward
for providing the right answers has changed.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.340
"How am I a part of this?"

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.540
"Oh you're really not as smart as I thought
you were."

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.220
If you manage to get all three riddles correct
— and there are only three riddles in total

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:50.060
— then you can unlock a secret image of
the Wayne family from before Bruce's parents'

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.060
death.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.160
The photo shows Thomas Wayne, Martha Wayne,
and a young Bruce — played by Luke Roberts,

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:59.760
Stella Stocker, and Oscar Novak, respectively
— relaxing on the floor in the lavishly

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.810
appointed living room of Wayne Manor.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:06.180
In the film, the Riddler's personal connection
to the Wayne family plays a major part in

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.180
his plan.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.580
So, it makes sense that one of the secrets
the Riddler reveals is connected to this part

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.950
of Bruce's past.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.560
The caption underneath the photo describes
the image as having been taken during Thomas

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.570
Wayne's mayoral campaign, while also mentioning
the Renewal Corporation, the latter of which

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:25.240
has plenty of significance in the plot of
"The Batman."

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:30.230
Meanwhile, the image file itself is named
"no me rompas," which translates from Spanish

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.130
into "do not break me."

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:36.370
Meanwhile, if you visit the site again after
you've solved the riddles and received the

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.490
first image, you'll also get another image
of a message in the Riddler's code.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.520
Can you solve it?

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.080
There could even be more on the site to discover
over the coming days and weeks, which might

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.870
either lead to additional material related
to "The Batman," or something that hints at

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.180
the Riddler's future…

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:55.260
"Please do not lie.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:04:01.420
What is the price for your blind eye?"

